configuration-and-targets.md:67: - A file may hold only `targets`, `chat`, `fleet` and `notes`. Each target may hold only `id`, `runtime`, `url`, `defaultModel`, `wireModels`, `capabilities`, `pricing` and `auth` with `apiKeyEnvVar` or `oauthProfile`; `chat` and `fleet` hold `target` (a target in the file) and an optional `model`. Any other key, such as a literal key (`auth.apiKey`), request `headers` or `safety` settings, refuses the whole file and names the key
